=== Implicit Type Coercion (writability UP, reliability DOWN) ===
  Python refuses '3' + 4: can only concatenate str (not "int") to str
  JavaScript would give '34' (string concat) - silent wrong type

=== List Comprehensions (writability UP, readability tradeoff) ===
  Loop:          [0, 4, 16, 36, 64]
  Comprehension: [0, 4, 16, 36, 64]
  Functional:    [0, 4, 16, 36, 64]
  Same answer, different readability/writability profiles
  Comprehensions come back in week 1: dict and set forms, laziness,
  and what the declarative style charges you for hiding the machinery.

=== Exception Handling (reliability UP, writability cost) ===
  safe_divide(10, 2) = 5.0
  unsafe_divide(10, 2) = 5.0
  safe_divide(10, 0) -> ZeroDivisionError: Cannot divide by zero
  unsafe_divide(10, 0) -> ZeroDivisionError: division by zero
  safe_divide('10', 2) -> TypeError: Expected number, got str
  unsafe_divide('10', 2) -> TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for /: 'str' and 'int'

=== Dynamic Dispatch (writability UP, reliability cost) ===
  Duck.sound() = 'quack'
  Dog.sound() = 'woof'
  Rock.sound() -> AttributeError: 'Rock' object has no attribute 'sound'
